{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And HaShem Elohim formed.</b> Elsewhere it says that the birds were created from the waters, and here it says from the earth — because there are species of birds that were created from the waters and their dwelling is there, such as ducks and divers, and there are other birds that were created from the earth and cannot survive in water, such as chickens and many other birds." "<b>And he brought to the man.</b> Fish he did not bring, for they are within the waters and do not come out, and if they come out they die, and he has no dominion over them. Also beasts he did not bring, because they were present with him and he was accustomed to them and recognized them, and there was no need to bring them to him." "<b>To see what he would call it.</b> To see what the living spirit that He breathed into his nostrils grasped — whether he would call the creatures names fitting for them, and he succeeded, as it is written, 'that was its name' — it is the name fitting for it, for his intellect concurred with the knowledge of his Creator." "<b>And whatsoever the man would call it,</b> etc. — so that he would know on his own to recall their names when he needed them. For if HaShem, may He be blessed, had called them names and taught them to the man, he would not have grasped the matter quickly, and it would have been hard for him to enter into the matter."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:34.425833927Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}